p that integrates well with HTML and CSS. Here\\\\u2019s an example of how you might use HubL: ```markdown --- title: My Page Title --- # Introduction This is a [header1](https://example.com/header1) section. ## Subsection 1 Subsection content goes here. Use *italic* or **bold** text for emphasis. ### Nested Section Nested section example: - Item 1 - Item 2 You can also use [links](https://www.example.com/), [code blocks](#), and even include images with: ![Alt Text](http://example/image.jpg) ## Table of Contents --- * Introduction * Subsection 1 * Nested Section ``` ### Markdown in HubL Examples: Markdown syntax can be used directly within a header or paragraph to format text. Here\\\\u2019s an example where Markdown is utilized for formatting: ```markdown --- # Header with Markdown Here\\'s some markdown code to format the header and section: - **Bold**: `**This is bold text**` - *Italic*: `*This is italic text*` ``` ### Link Example: Links can be created using HTML attributes within HubL, like this: ```markdown [Link](http://example.com) Or you can create an internal link to another part of the same page: [Internal Link](#section1) ``` Remember that HubL is intended for web pages and not necessarily every element on a web page. It\\\\u2019s best used within header elements or after markdown links. Please let me know if there are any specific modules or functionalities you want assistance with, or if this explanation was helpful!\"}]}', 'conversation_memory_persist:3027bcaf-eeaf-4746-8d55-0390d9f922e6:c779ad33-2267-4643-a4d0-f0e3863d730e:c2458f571bd4', 0, 1, None, None, None, None, '2026-04-19 04:20:52.525829', '2026-04-19 04:20:52.525832', '2026-04-19 04:20:52.525834', None))"}
