02269268036, -0.02508673071861267, -0.010276151821017265, 0.08217121660709381, -0.0033187370281666517, -0.08280616998672485, -0.0913604274392128, -0.012519178912043571, 0.0656735971570015, 0.006126532796770334, 0.06995181739330292, -0.006214572582393885, -0.04153979569673538, -0.05408407747745514, 0.022984642535448074, 0.04251449555158615, -0.023754285648465157, -0.017582479864358902, -0.04700254276394844, -0.015581178478896618, 0.03697149083018303, 0.12488164752721786, 0.055120356380939484, -0.039681002497673035, -0.029805587604641914, -0.010888438671827316, 0.018076393753290176, 0.018115462735295296, 0.00957848597317934, 0.06784849613904953, -0.014248434454202652, 0.09044212102890015, 0.031401533633470535, 0.14479374885559082, -0.06464065611362457, 0.1060224175453186, -0.025452667847275734, -0.050188422203063965, 0.013285473920404911, -0.06316116452217102, -0.05573878809809685, -0.08032294362783432, 0.03030109778046608, 0.01795099303126335, -0.09591224789619446, 0.03248051181435585, 0.04977201297879219, 0.016955086961388588, -0.011399175971746445, 0.05743803083896637, -0.004628835245966911, -0.016027318313717842, -0.00993794109672308, -0.004720127675682306, -0.034495770931243896, 0.033134378492832184, 0.03326907008886337, 0.03798796981573105], \"response_payload\": {\"response\": \"HubSpot Markup Language (HubL) is a custom syntax that enables developers to add features specific to your website or application directly into the main content of your web pages using Markdown formatting. This allows for cleaner, more semantic markup that integrates well with HTML and CSS.\\\\n\\\\nHere\\\\u2019s an example of how you might use HubL:\\\\n\\\\n```markdown\\\\n---\\\\ntitle: My Page Title\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# Introduction\\\\n\\\\nThis is a [header1](https://example.com/header1) section.\\\\n\\\\n## Subsection 1\\\\n\\\\nSubsection content goes here. Use *italic* or **bold** text for emphasis.\\\\n\\\\n### Nested Section\\\\n\\\\nNested section example:\\\\n- Item 1\\\\n- Item 2\\\\n\\\\nYou can also use [links](https://www.example.com/), [code blocks](#),\\\\nand even include images with:\\\\n\\\\n![Alt Text](http://example/image.jpg)\\\\n\\\\n## Table of Contents\\\\n---\\\\n* Introduction\\\\n* Subsection 1\\\\n* Nested Section\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Markdown in HubL Examples:\\\\nMarkdown syntax can be used directly within a header or paragraph to format text. Here\\\\u2019s an example where Markdown is utilized for formatting:\\\\n\\\\n```markdown\\\\n---\\\\n\\\\n# Header with Markdown\\\\n\\\\nHere\\'s some markdown code to format the header and section:\\\\n\\\\n- **Bold**: `**This is bold text**`\\\\n- *Italic*: `*This is italic text*`\\\\n\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\n### Link Example:\\\\nLinks can be created using HTML attributes within HubL, like this:\\\\n\\\\n```markdown\\\\n[Link](http://example.com)\\\\n\\\\nOr you can create an internal link to another part of the same page:\\\\n\\\\n[Internal Link](#section1)\\\\n```\\\\n\\\\nRemember that HubL is intended for web pages and not necessarily every element on a web page. It\\\\u2019s best used within header elements or after markdown links.\\\\n\\\\nPlease let me know if there are any specific modules or functionalities you want assistance with, or if this explanation was helpful!\", \"status_message\": \"completed_with_fallback\", \"quick_chips\": [], \"tool_events\": [], \"pending_tool_actions\": []}}', 'semantic_cache_fill:3027bcaf-eeaf-4746-8d55-0390d9f922e6:local:legacy:d81f13f5a93d35a9862992f3939ef56d8334fbed44d01d5cfedbb333189f5abb', 0, 1, None, None, None, None, '2026-04-19 04:20:52.646142', '2026-04-19 04:20:52.646147', '2026-04-19 04:20:52.646151', None)) completed"}
