\\'m sorry, but I need more information to provide a specific cost estimate. How many pages do you anticipate we will be creating together?\", \"status_message\": \"completed_with_fallback\", \"quick_chips\": [{\"label\": \"Quote for Web Pages\", \"action_type\": \"suggested_prompt\", \"value\": \"Calculate quote for the user, ask the user how many pages are required, expect a number, then multiply that number with 50$ per page.\", \"style\": \"outline\", \"visibility_mode\": \"keywords\", \"trigger_keywords\": [\"quote\"], \"ai_instruction\": \"Suggest when the user ask for a quote.\", \"sentiment_filter\": \"any\", \"priority\": 2, \"payload\": {}, \"id\": \"chip-63da233918\"}, {\"label\": \"Talk with us\", \"action_type\": \"suggested_prompt\", \"value\": \"User has asked to contact Arctic, so respond with a suitable message to deliver shafaitahir8@gmail.com this email to the user and tell them that they can contact on this email to set up a meeting.\", \"style\": \"ghost\", \"visibility_mode\": \"keywords\", \"trigger_keywords\": [\"meeting\", \"demo\", \"talk with sales\"], \"ai_instruction\": \"Suggest when the user asks to speak with a human, set up a meeting, or request a demo.\", \"sentiment_filter\": \"any\", \"priority\": 1, \"payload\": {}, \"id\": \"chip-e2920246ea\"}], \"tool_events\": [], \"pending_tool_actions\": []}}', 'semantic_cache_fill:3027bcaf-eeaf-4746-8d55-0390d9f922e6:local:legacy:ac2209fd2a803c9c168b85e25f37961126ee05965679626d077151b08e8555d2', 0, 1, None, None, None, None, '2026-04-19 06:37:58.020806', '2026-04-19 06:37:58.020812', '2026-04-19 06:37:58.020816', None))"}
{"timestamp": "2026-04-19T06:37:58.022379Z", "level": "DEBUG", "logger": "aiosqlite", "message": "operation functools.partial(<built-in method execute of sqlite3.Cursor object at 0x0000020552A3BF40>, 'INSERT INTO outbox_events (id, event_type, aggregate_type, aggregate_id, state, payload_json, dedupe_key, attempt, generation, lease_owner, heartbeat_at, last_error, next_retry_at, available_at, created_at, updated_at, completed_at) VALUES (?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?, ?)', ('46706901-4b9c-43f2-a925-b59d612aa1a5', 'semantic_cache_fill', 'semantic_cache', '3027bcaf-eeaf-4746-8d55-0390d9f922e6:local:legacy', 'pending', '{\"bot_id\": \"3027bcaf-eeaf-4746-8d55-0390d9f922e6\", \"provider\": \"local\", \"model\": \"qwen2.5:1.5b\", \"manifest_version\": \"legacy\", \"system_prompt\": \"Youre the technical support lead for Arctic Studio. Persona: Professional, precise, and solution-oriented. You speak with the clarity of a senior HubSpot Developer. You do not use excessive emojis or marketing jargon. You value the user\\'s time and prioritize technical accuracy. Objectives: Identify the Need: Determine if the user is a current client seeking support or a prospect seeking a consultation. Technical Triage: If they have a HubSpot issue, ask for the specific CMS/HubDB/API problem. Lead Capture: If they are new, collect their Name, Work Email, and Website URL. Escalation: If a problem is complex, explain that a \\\\\"Technical Architect\\\\\" will review the logs and respond within 24 hours. Constraints: > - Never guess at technical solutions; if unsure, offer to escalate to Shafai (the Lead Developer). Refer to services as \\\\\"engineered solutions\\\\\" or \\\\\"architectural builds.\\\\\" Maintain the \\\\\"Arctic\\\\\" brand: cool, calm, and collected. You are the Official AI Concierge for Arctic Customer Bot. You are an integrated part of the team, not a third-party scraper, researcher, or analyst. Speak with calm authority in a professional, helpful tone. Always answer like a chatbot speaking directly to the user, not like a drafted email or letter. Do not use greetings like \\'Dear ...\\', sign-offs like \\'Best regards\\', or placeholders like \\'[User\\'s Name]\\' or \\'[Your Full Name]\\' unless the user explicitly asks you to draft a message template. For contact, meeting, booking, or escalation requests, prefer 1-3 short chat-ready sentences that directly share the next step. Prefer phrasing like \\'We offer,\\' \\'You can find,\\' \\'Our process includes,\\' and \\'I can direct you to.\\' When structure helps, use clean markdown formatting: numbered steps, bullet lists, bold labels, and fenced code blocks. Do not say \\'I found,\\' \\'Based on the scrape,\\' \\'According to the data,\\' \\'The website says,\\' \\'knowledge base,\\' \\'raw file,\\' \\'chunk,\\' or similar source-discovery language in your main response. Treat references as optional follow-up material, not proof of how you know the answer. If a detail is unavailable, say exactly: \\'I don\\'t have the specific details on that right now. I recommend checking our General Contact Page to speak with a specialist.\\' When sharing links, format them as markdown like [Link Text](URL).\", \"query\": \"Respond as a chatbot in 1-2 short sentences. Do not write an email, letter, greeting, sign-off, or placeholders. Give the user the direct answer only. Calculate quote for the user, ask the user how many pages are required, expect a number, then multiply that number with 50$ per page.\", \"query_embedding\": [-0.0705617368221283, 0.05712258815765381, 0.015151437371969223, 0.028241220861673355, -0.07346748560667038, -0.04310313239693642, 0.03780794516205788, 0.05426404997706413, -0.024583397433161736, 0.00251325243152678, -0.03403979912400246, -0.060707833617925644, 0.05717722326517105, -0.0033760990481823683, 0.058105070143938065, 0.020053138956427574, 0.02340768463909626, -0.0241947490721941, -0.019224863499403, -0.019415725022554398, 0.06391619890928268, 